# NOTICE - third-party software and data shipped with OREOA-AI platform v2

OREOA-AI platform v2 (the repository content: source code, prompts, tests,
corpus generators, mappings) is licensed under **AGPL-3.0** (see `LICENSE`).
Third-party components listed below are used by **simple aggregation**: they
run as separate programs or are consumed as data, with no code linking, and
keep their own licences. Distribution of the container images (binary
distribution) triggers the licence notices below.

Three distribution models are used, and they matter for compliance:

1. **Baked into images** (sections 2-4): shipped inside the container images
   built from this repository.
2. **One-shot build/refresh images** (section 5): pulled or built on the
   analyst's workstation, never shipped inside the platform images.
3. **Knowledge and rule sets - never baked** (section 6): fetched on the
   analyst's workstation by `make update-knowledge` at pinned commits,
   recorded in `knowledge/snapshot.json`, and mounted read-only into the
   containers. No image contains them; a recipient re-fetches the pinned
   sources themselves.

Exact in-image inventory: per-package licence texts live inside each image
(`/usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/*.dist-info` and
`/usr/share/doc/*/copyright`). A generated SBOM per image (syft) lands at
work-order step 2 (CI matrix). Versions below are the `versions.env` pins at
the time of this regeneration; every pin bump is a PR that reviews this file.

